@page "/About"
@layout MainLayout

<PageTitle>About - PresDB</PageTitle>

<div class="mb-4">
    <p class="text-uppercase text-muted small fw-semibold mb-1">CEDAC Preservation Database</p>
    <h1 class="h2 mb-1">About and Documentation</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
        A guide to the WebPresDB website, preservation assessment, data workflows, and notice archive.
    </p>
    <div class="small text-muted mt-2">Last updated November 18, 2026</div>
</div>



<section id="website" class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">Overview</h2>
    <p>CEDAC's Preservation Database is a tool designed for tracking the affordablily status of housing projects across
        Massachusetts. To achive this goal, the database collects and maintains data from serval public and internal
        sources, linking them to a singular property record. CEDAC publishes an official preservation forecast report
        bi-anualy that derives from the information inside of this database. This website includes features to search,
        inspect source records, generate reports, and manage 40T notices.</p>

        

                    <section id="property-search" class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="h4">Property search and details</h2>
                        <p>
                            The home page searches the properties table using a project name or general term, city, Property ID,
                            or HUD contract program type. Searches with text are automatically repeated after a short typing delay;
                            the search button also performs an immediate search.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Selecting a result opens the property inspector. The inspector summarizes unit counts, restrictions,
                            organization names, comments, and source-specific unit counts. Its tabs organize linked records,
                            including HUD property and contract records, LIHTC, DHCD, HUD active and terminated mortgages,
                            USDA, MHP, MassHousing FOA, PBV, and at-risk or comment information.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section id="reports" class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="h4">Reports</h2>

                        <h3 class="h5 mt-3">Preservation report</h3>
                        <p>
                            A preservation report evaluates every property at a selected forecast date. The report can use the
                            most recent import or the oldest available import for archive-backed fields. It returns each property's
                            status, matching preservation rule or override, unit counts, and preserved-through date.
                        </p>
                        <div class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm table-bordered align-middle">
                                <thead class="table-dark">
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Status</th>
                                        <th>Meaning</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><span class="badge text-bg-success">Preserved</span></td>
                                        <td>A preservation rule matched for the forecast date.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                    <tr>
                                        <td><span class="badge text-bg-danger">At risk</span></td>
                                        <td>No preservation rule matched, or an at-risk date override takes precedence.</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Custom report</h3>
                        <p>
                            A custom report starts with Property ID and lets the user select additional fields from the report field
                            catalog, search for fields, change column order, and download the result as CSV. The same most-recent or
                            oldest-available snapshot option is available, with an optional filter for properties that have DHCD award
                            records.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Past reports</h3>
                        <p>
                            Past Reports lists official preservation PDFs from the report archive. Each entry can be opened in a new browser
                            tab.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section id="decision-tree" class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="h4">Preservation decision tree</h2>
                        <p>
                            The decision tree is a rule-based screening tool used by preservation reports. It does not make a legal
                            determination; it records the rule or override that the current dataset used to classify a property at the
                            selected forecast date. Rules are evaluated in the order listed below, and the first matching rule is shown.
                        </p>

                        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered mb-3">
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>Title VI override.</strong>
                                A property marked Title II/VI as <strong>VI</strong> is preserved when the forecast date is on or before
                                January 1, 2043.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>Title II override.</strong>
                                A property marked as <strong>II</strong> is preserved only when its Title II at-risk date is on or before
                                the forecast date.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>Active HUD mortgage section of act.</strong>
                                A current mortgage with section code YHE or YHN is preserved only if its final endorsement date is within 15
                                years of the forecast date.
                                Codes ZPC, ZPD, ZPE, ZPF, ZPH, or ZPI preserve the property regardless of endorsement date.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>HUD mortgage category or endorsement date.</strong>
                                An active mortgage with SOA category <strong>236(j)(1)</strong> or <strong>202 Elderly</strong> preserves
                                the property.
                                A mortgage is also preserved when its final endorsement date is within 15 years of the forecast date.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>HUD contract expiration.</strong>
                                A HUD contract whose TRACS overall expiration date is on or after the forecast date preserves the property.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>PRAC or 202 HUD contract.</strong>
                                A HUD contract with <strong>PRAC</strong> or <strong>202</strong> in the program type group code field from
                                HUD contracts feed preserves
                                the property.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>LIHTC award year.</strong>
                                A property with a yr_pis or yr_alloc from the LIHTC feed that is that is less than 30 years ago will
                                preserve the property as LIHTC restrctions have a minimum term of 30 years.

                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>Preserved-through date.</strong>
                                A preserved-unit aging record preserves the property if its preserved-through date is on or after the
                                forecast date and its units-at-risk value is zero or blank.
                            </li>
                            <li class="list-group-item">
                                <strong>Overrides.</strong>
                                At-risk date overrides are manually entered by a CEDAC staff member. If the property's at-risk date override
                                is on or after the forecast date,the property is considered preserved and that date is reported as the
                                preserving rule.
                            </li>
                        </ol>

                        <div class="alert alert-danger mb-0">
                            <strong>At-risk override:</strong> if the property's at-risk date override is before the forecast date,
                            the property is marked at risk regardless of another matching preservation rule. If no rule or qualifying
                            override matches, the property is marked at risk with “No preservation rule matched.”
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <section id="40t-notices" class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="h4">40T notice system</h2>
                        <p>
                            The 40T page displays folders in the configured notice storage area. A folder is considered matched when
                            text before the first hyphen is an integer Property ID and that ID exists in the properties table.
                            Matched folders show the linked property; unmatched folders are listed separately.
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>The main page searches matched folders by Property ID, folder name, or linked property search text and shows
                                up to 100 folders unless a search is entered.</li>
                                <li>Opening a folder shows all PDF files and attempts to read a notice date from the file name.</li>
                                <li>The PDF viewer is available to users with database read access.</li>
                                <li>Only administrators can upload or delete notice PDFs. Uploads must be PDF files no larger than 100 MB, and
                                    existing file names are not overwritten.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </section>

                            <section id="imports" class="mb-4">
                                <h2 class="h4">Data imports</h2>
                                <p>
                                    The Import page is available to users with database edit access. It reviews the newest batch loaded for
                                    each configured archive source. Existing linked rows are not changed.
                                </p>
                                <ol>
                                    <li>Choose a configured data source and upload a CSV whose headers match the accepted archive columns.</li>
                                    <li>Review rows in the newest batch that have not been linked, ignored, or connected to a property.</li>
                                    <li>Enter an existing Property ID and link the row, create and link a new property, or mark the row as ignored.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>Export unmatched rows to CSV when a review needs to continue outside the website.</li>
                                </ol>
                                <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                                    Archive selections control which snapshot is displayed or reported. Database migrations and restore/import
                                    operations remain separate administrative processes and are not performed by the report screen.
                                </p>
                            </section>

                            <section id="access" class="mb-4">
                                <h2 class="h4">Accounts and access</h2>
                                <p>
                                    Authentication uses Microsoft identity when enabled. The application has three database roles:
                                </p>
                                <div class="table-responsive">
                                    <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
                                        <thead class="table-dark">
                                            <tr>
                                                <th>Role</th>
                                                <th>Typical access</th>
                                            </tr>
                                        </thead>
                                        <tbody>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><code>ExpUseDB_Read</code></td>
                                                <td>Search and open properties, view reports and 40T notices.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><code>ExpUseDB_Edit</code></td>
                                                <td>Read access plus import review and property-link actions.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td><code>ExpUseDB_Admin</code></td>
                                                <td>Edit access plus 40T notice upload and deletion actions.</td>
                                            </tr>
                                        </tbody>
                                    </table>
                                </div>
                                <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                                    Development configurations may disable authentication and provide a development identity with all three roles.
                                </p>
                            </section>
